"""Editorial question designs for textile history, weaving, and embroidery."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


TEXTILE_HISTORY = """history_origins|An Early Textile Record|What dated fabric or document establishes one local textile form?|Distinguish survival from absolute beginning.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Cloth Reexamined|What does one textile reveal about makers and use?|Check fiber, technique, owner, occasion, and provenance.
hidden_stories|Labor Behind a Textile|Whose growing, spinning, dyeing, weaving, and selling is uncredited?|Use archival and consented maker accounts.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Historic Cloth|How do fiber, structure, pattern, and use fit together?|Define object, place, period, and source limits.
advanced_concepts|Trade Versus Local Making|Can a textile's material and technique locate its production?|Compare analysis, trade records, and maker knowledge.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unknown Textile Workshop|Which evidence could identify maker or date?|Check weave, dyes, labels, provenance, and gaps.
technology_innovation|A Loom or Dye Transition|How did one change affect work and cloth?|Compare productivity, wages, design, and access.
people_personalities|A Textile Organizer's Role|How did one maker or merchant change production?|Use dated records and account for collective labor.
major_events|A Trade Shock in Cloth|How did one policy or disruption alter supply?|Trace prices, output, workers, and substitutes.
how_it_works|Tracing a Textile Chain|How did fiber become fabric and reach users?|Follow growing, spinning, dyeing, weaving, transport, and sale.
rise_fall|A Fabric's Changing Market|What explains a documented production trend?|Check demand, imports, machines, labor, and definitions.
then_vs_now|One Textile Across Eras|How did material, making, and meaning change?|Compare provenanced objects and living practice.
future_developments|What Evidence Is Still Missing|Which archives or objects could revise this history?|Identify access, permissions, and analytical limits.
myths_vs_facts|A Cloth from One Place Only?|Does a claimed geographic origin fit the evidence?|Separate motif resemblance from provenanced manufacture.
documentary_stories|One Cloth's Recorded Journey|How did it move from maker to current holder?|Build an ownership and use timeline.
creative_brief|A Historic Commission|What did patron, function, and maker negotiate?|Use contracts, sketches, and finished object where available.
materials_and_tools|Fiber and Dye in Context|Why were particular inputs available?|Trace ecology, cultivation, trade, and labor.
process_breakdown|Reconstructing Making Steps|Which steps are evidenced and which inferred?|Compare object analysis with maker testimony.
composition_choice|Pattern with a Purpose|Why might a layout fit its intended use?|Attribute period and practitioner explanations; mark inference.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made the Cloth|How were design, yarn, weaving, and finishing divided?|Trace credits and wages, including invisible work.
adaptation_across_media|Pattern to Printed Reproduction|What was lost or changed when a textile became an image?|Compare scale, color, texture, and rights.
audience_reception|Changing Values of One Cloth|How did users, collectors, and museums describe it?|Use dated accounts and their interests.
cultural_context|Use Beyond Display|What social role did a textile have at a named time?|Use owner and community evidence, respecting restricted meanings.
preservation_restoration|A Historic Fabric's Care|How have storage and treatment altered its evidence?|Review conservation history and owner priorities.
rights_and_attribution|Textile Designs and Ownership|Who may reproduce a historic pattern today?|Check maker descendants, communities, contracts, and law.
style_comparison|Two Fabrics, Similar Motifs|What differs in structure, material, date, and use?|Compare provenanced samples before claims of copying.
creative_failure|A Failed Textile Experiment|What can surviving trials tell us about production?|Use documented samples and avoid hindsight assumptions.
field_community_ownership|Whose Textile History|Who should control access to records and designs?|Consult maker communities and custodians.
field_object_provenance|A Cloth's Custody Chain|Where are acquisition and ownership gaps?|Trace receipts, labels, transfers, and disputes.
field_living_practice|Historical Skill Today|Which techniques remain in use or have changed?|Ask current makers without treating them as frozen evidence.
field_conservation_choice|Object or Skill|What preservation priority do makers and holders prefer?|Compare storage, repair, apprenticeship, and access.
field_cultural_translation|A Pattern's Name|How do original terms differ from catalog labels?|Attribute speakers and translation choices.
"""

